  "worked_solution": "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is \n\n$$\nb=AB=5\\,\\text{m}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is \n\n$$\nh=12\\,\\text{m}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 12}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{60}{2} \\\\  & =30\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
